va","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"File impact set; starting plan review.","timestamp":1794481982256727001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Commit 23b4a112383. RED: 7 of 9 tests in the new tests/unit/test_bedrock_cache_capability.py fail on the pre-fix tree, including the end-to-end run (qwen via the real provider builder, 20,000 input tokens, zero cache counters) that logged the false cache-ineffective warning; all 9 pass after. 270 tests across the capability, cache, structured-output, provenance and bedrock suites pass. make verify running.","timestamp":1794482914101383001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Commit 23b4a112383: make verify exit 0, 03:28-05:27 PST 2026-11-12 (21178 passed, 29 skipped; integration 218 passed, 2 skipped). Pushed for review.","timestamp":1794490084181623001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Gerrit 3372: Verified +1; LLM-Review -1 is the fail-closed coverage gap from the Bedrock spend cap (BedrockDailySpendCapDeny attached; lifts 00:00 UTC = 16:00 PST), not a code finding. Next: after the cap lifts, comment rerun-llm-review on 3372, then safe-submit and close.","timestamp":1794492313426508001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"HANDOFF STATE 2026-11-12 06:45 PST (session 3d705fec): in_progress, held. Gerrit 3372 (commit 23b4a112383) is pushed; Verified +1, LLM-Review -1 (spend cap). Blocked: the Bedrock daily spend cap (BedrockDailySpendCapDeny) is attached to the review bot's role (rebar-gerrit-instance-role) and to the lmn production roles, so LLM-Review casts a fail-closed coverage-gap -1 with no code findings. It lifts automatically at 00:00 UTC (16:00 PST). Lifting it early is a spend-policy call, so it is left for the operator. Remaining steps, in order: after 16:00 PST, comment `rerun-llm-review` on 3372 if the vote is still the coverage gap; at LLM-Review +1 / Verified +1 / 0 unresolved, run scripts/gerrit_safe_submit.py 3372 --revision <current sha>; fast-forward the worktree; post completion evidence, tick the AC boxes, and close with `--class preexisting`.","timestamp":1794494776387471001}],"created_at":1794466839457769001,"creation_channel":"python","deps":[{"link_uuid":"f1db48f6-0efb-4042-b434-762f6d8aa623","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"a81a-946a-31c9-4d03"},{"link_uuid":"c24cc185-0531-4bbd-85b7-acea6fb94c7d","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"54fd-316c-7072-4611"}],"description":"## Observation\n\n`capabilities._capabilities_from_profile` classifies every profile exposing `bedrock_supports_prompt_caching` as `prompt_cache_style=\"bedrock\"`, whatever that flag's value. `cache_settings_for` then returns Bedrock cache settings, and `runner.py` passes `caching_requested=cache_settings is not None` to `cache_diagnostics.warn_if_cache_ineffective`. pydantic-ai 1.107.9 applies those settings only when the profile's `bedrock_supports_prompt_caching` / `bedrock_supports_tool_caching` is True (models/bedrock.py 894-895, 1102-1103, 1117-1118). For a vendor whose flag is False no cache point is sent, both counters are 0, and any call at or above the cache floor logs \"prompt caching requested ... but had NO effect\" although caching was never possible.\n\nMeasured 2026-11-12 from pydantic-ai 1.107.9's `BedrockProvider.model_profile` (plus rebar's wrap from garlicky-leery-seal for meta and unknown vendors):\n- Caching (`bedrock_supports_prompt_caching=True`): anthropic, amazon.nova. The ticket's original list wrongly included nova; nova caches prompts (not tools).\n- Not caching (False): mistral, cohere, deepseek, openai on Bedrock, qwen, google, minimax, nvidia, meta, unknown vendors.\n- Native structured output is True for qwen, google, minimax and nvidia while caching is False, so `prompt_cache_style` must stay `bedrock` for them: `structured.native_output_stack_supported` uses it to apply the botocore `outputConfig` check.\n\n## Approach\n\n1. `src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py`:\n   - Add `prompt_caching: bool = True` to `ModelCapabilities`: whether this model can cache prompts at all.\n   - `_capabilities_from_profile` sets it from `bedrock_supports_prompt_caching` for a Bedrock profile; other styles keep True. `prompt_cache_style` is unchanged for every profile.\n   - `cache_settings_for` returns `None` for the `bedrock` style when `prompt_caching` is False. The runner then sends no `bedrock_cache_*` settings and passes `caching_requested=False`, so the warning stays silent. A caching model's settings are unchanged.\n2. `src/rebar/llm/runner_support.py`: the fallback-chain merge carries `prompt_caching` from the primary, as it does `prompt_cache_style` (the cache directive follows the primary, bug 96f3).\nNo config key, env var or flag.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py`\n- `src/rebar/llm/runner_support.py`\n- `tests/unit/test_bedrock_cache_capability.py` (new)\n\n## Testing\n\n- RED then GREEN, new file:\n  - For mistral, qwen and meta Bedrock ids, `prompt_caching` is False, `prompt_cache_style` stays `bedrock`, and `cache_settings_for` returns None in both execution modes. Fails pre-fix (settings returned).\n  - For an anthropic Bedrock id and nova-pro, `prompt_caching` is True and `cache_settings_for` returns the same settings as today.\n  - End to end through `PydanticAIRunner` with a scripted Converse client (the real provider builder, only boto3's session replaced): a qwen run whose usage reports input above the floor and zero cache counters logs no cache-ineffective warning, and the request carries no `cachePoint`. Fails pre-fix (warning logged).\n  - The same run for an anthropic Bedrock id with zero counters still warns.\n  - The chain merge takes `prompt_caching` from the primary.\n- Existing capability, cache and structured-output tests stay green (`test_llm_capabilities.py`, `test_agentic_message_cache.py`, `test_runner_support.py`, `test_structured.py`, `test_verdict_provenance.py`).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A Bedrock model whose profile has `bedrock_supports_prompt_caching=False` produces no cache-ineffective warning, shown by a test.\n- [ ] A caching Bedrock model with both counters at 0 above the floor still warns.\n- [ ] Non-caching Bedrock models keep `prompt_cache_style=\"bedrock\"`, so native structured-output routing is unchanged, shown by a test.\n- [ ] The fallback-chain merge carries `prompt_caching` from the primary, shown by a test.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] `env -u JIRA_URL -u JIRA_USER -u JIRA_API_TOKEN make verify` exits 0 on the commit pushed for review.\n  provenance: environment=macOS dev host, fix-swellfish worktree; principal=Rebar Bot Nava; privilege_posture=narrower; instrument=live-call — exit status and log live outside the repository\n","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py","reason":"prompt_caching capability; no cache settings for non-caching Bedrock models"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/runner_support.py","reason":"chain merge carries prompt_caching from the primary"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_bedrock_cache_capability.py","reason":"regression tests"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","54fd-316c-7072-4611"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"a35fc59c-0cd8-4ba1-a89e-4f44f281147f","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"b26e-757e-bca5-4b5b","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Cache-ineffective warning fires on Bedrock vendors that have no prompt caching","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["990de776-a9ab-4adf-9e83-b554542809b1","ab4f37ce-03e9-464c-bd2a-a372557d9b15","e5b43c14-bbad-4241-8560-647799b75b01","7d203555-44b3-4558-b7c8-c2433d50a9b8","7a4ee83d-0489-4643-ba8f-ede17ab3f296","a35fc59c-0cd8-4ba1-a89e-4f44f281147f","e5b6fdd3-86cb-40a0-8332-96898ca47068","11628482-7f87-4058-8823-fef2386fbd71","d83eb814-3352-4e9c-9d6f-2a48555a9d09","c24cc185-0531-4bbd-85b7-acea6fb94c7d","86729ddf-fc7b-4a6d-a8b9-fbc29c1588de","487f5f06-f577-4c3d-a79f-10c830ad0602"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794494776387471002,"uuid":"9356e907-5c52-491b-99a7-f62450e765c8"}